WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.139
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:07.830
A lot of things that you would naturally assume
are against the law, aren't in many parts

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.160
of the world.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:16.720
There are some really strange, and often disturbing
things that you can legally get away with.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:22.230
First up is cannibalism.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:27.890
Yes you heard that right, in most countries
around the world, including the United States

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:34.250
and most of Europe, there are no outright
laws against the consumption of human flesh.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.579
In most cases cannibals are charged with murder.

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:43.039
However if someone willingly gives you permission
to hack off a piece of their flesh and eat

00:00:43.039 --> 00:00:47.680
it, you're strangely not doing anything illegal.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.590
Have you ever wanted to own a tiger?

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:56.870
Well you're in luck, it's illegal to own a
tiger in the UK under the Dangerous Wild Animals

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:57.870
Act.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:04.560
But in Canada and several US states it's completely
fine in the eyes of the law to go online and

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.270
buy a tiger then bring it home, which is easier
than you may think.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:15.250
In case you were wondering a baby bengal tiger
will cost you around $1,000.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:21.470
In 14 US states it's legal to own a tiger,
however you are required to register for a

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.150
permit to own large cats.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:30.450
However in 9 states there are no laws against
it whatsoever, you can just go ahead and buy

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:35.080
one, despite the significant risks they can
pose to the public.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:42.030
In fact there are currently 12,000 privately
owned pet tigers in America, and that excludes

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.950
the ones kept in zoos.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.110
Next up is radar detectors.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:51.720
These nifty little boxes sit on your car's
dashboard and will alert you if your speed

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:57.060
is being monitored by the police using a radar
gun, so you can slow down.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:01.900
It's obvious to see why many people think
they're illegal, since they allow you to thwart

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:03.271
the cop's law enforcement methods.

00:02:03.271 --> 00:02:04.271
But surprisingly, they're not.

00:02:04.271 --> 00:02:06.070
At least not in most countries.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:13.090
They're completely legal in most of of Australia,
some areas of Canada, all of Russia, all of

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:20.160
the United Kingdom and all of the United States
except from Washington DC and Virginia.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:25.500
However don't get radar detectors mixed up
with radar jammers, those are devices that

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.860
jam police radar signals, preventing them
from working full stop, and these are very

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:39.200
much illegal, using one will land you with
a $1,000 fine and one year behind bars.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.200
On the subject of driving.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:47.160
Contrary to popular belief it's completely
legal to drive barefoot.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:52.760
That's right you can leave your shoes at home
and legally drive a car in most countries,

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.710
including the United Kingdom, Canada and the
US.

00:02:56.710 --> 00:03:03.090
Although driving barefoot isn't as safe as
wearing shoes, so a lot of traffic enforcement

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:09.280
officers will try to tell you off for it anyway,
despite it being legal.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.400
We all know that breaking and entering is
illegal.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.560
So you would be forgiven if you thought that
owning and using lock picks is illegal.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:21.660
But turns out, it's one hundred percent legal.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:27.130
In most countries it's completely legal to
own and use lock picks, as long as you're

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:31.550
not using them to trespass on other people's
private property.

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:36.970
Most countries however, do have a law against
going equipped for theft, that means if a

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:41.790
police officer pulls you over at 3am and you
have a balaclava and a set of lock picks in

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:47.459
your car, that qualifies as going equipped
for theft and you're probably going down the

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:48.930
nick.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:56.360
If that surprises you, how about this: In
America it's also legal to own a flamethrower.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:02.160
In most countries, these fossil-fuel-burning
weapons of destruction are outright banned.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:08.130
In the UK for example you will receive 5 years
in prison if you're simply caught with a flamethrower

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:09.260
in your possession.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:15.640
But in the United States there is no federal
law against the possession and use of a flamethrower,

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:18.350
regardless of how powerful it is.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:23.100
It's not just a deadly weapon though, in certain
states in the south of the United States and

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.380
in some south American countries.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:31.450
flamethrowers are used to fend off deadly
attacks on humans from Africanised Honey Bees,

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.540
otherwise known as killer bees.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:39.740
Yes you can legally own a flamethrower, but
that's not the only deadly weapon you can

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.070
legally own.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:42.770
How about a tank?

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:46.520
Yes, in most countries you can legally own
a tank.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:51.730
However don't get too excited, you can't go
all grand theft auto on innocent civilians.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:55.850
The law requires the tank's cannon to be deactivated.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:05:01.380
If you replace the steel tracks with rubber
tracks and obtain a certain permit you can

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:05.600
also legally drive your brand new tank on
the road.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:08.350
Tanks are also surprisingly affordable.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:13.880
You can pickup an ex-soviet tank for around
$40,000.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:20.100
Corporal punishment in schools was outlawed
in the United Kingdom in 1987 and in Australia

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.580
in 1985.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:28.750
However, to many people's surprise corporal
punishment is still completely legal in 19

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.160
states in America.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:36.740
19 states including Texas, Alabama, Florida
and Kentucky still allow a teacher or principal

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:41.560
to punish public school students by hitting
them repeatedly.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:47.490
In practice corporal punishment is becoming
increasingly less common in the United States,

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:53.730
however a report in 2011 showed that one Texas
school administered corporal punishment to

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:58.610
over 120 different kids in that year alone.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:04.280
The most common form of corporal punishment
in the US is paddling, where a student is

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:10.290
hit multiple times on their buttocks or thighs
with a wooden paddle, however in many such

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:14.669
schools paddles are made from shaved down
baseball bats.

00:06:14.669 --> 00:06:20.500
We've all seen the films and TV shows where
clever criminals count cards during casino

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:26.710
blackjack games to cheat the house and net
large wins, before being beat up and thrown

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:29.300
out by the casino's security team.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:34.220
Television therefore has made it quite obvious
that card counting is illegal.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:35.960
Or is it?

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:43.620
Well, turns out it isn't, card counting is
completely legal in the majority of countries,

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:47.490
including the United Kingdom and the United
States.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:51.360
Card counting is a blackjack technique where
players count the cards that have already

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:56.540
been played to try and predict what the dealer's
next hand is likely to be.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:07:01.610
It's widely considered as cheating and most
casinos will actively try to deter players

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:07.040
from counting cards by harassing players,
changing the percentage of cards in the deck

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:10.620
or using extremely high speed dealers.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:15.610
Casinos are completely within their rights
to ban you for this, but it's certainly not

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:16.630
illegal.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:23.960
And finally, it's not just card counting that
films and TV has led us to believe is against

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:24.960
the law.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:30.180
As a result of it happening constantly on
TV most people believe that an undercover

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:35.570
police officer is required by law to identify
themselves when asked.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:38.600
But it's simply not true.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:43.710
A police officer is legally allowed to lie
about their status and basically anything

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:46.839
else they like whilst they are undercover.

00:07:46.839 --> 00:07:52.180
They are even allowed to fabricate facts and
stories to get information.

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:58.240
Police do however have to identify themselves
to you if they're in uniform or taking legal

00:07:58.240 --> 00:07:59.530
action against you.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:02.759
Thanks for the view, subscribe for more Thoughty2.

